  "text": "Key date\n1916-D Mercury Dime Value\nThe 1916-D is the key date of the Mercury dime series. With a mintage of just 264,000 from the Denver mint, it is scarce in every grade and one of the most counterfeited US coins.\nKey facts\nMintage: only 264,000 — by far the lowest of the series.\nComposition: 90% silver (≈0.0723 oz), so it also carries melt value.\nHeavily faked, often by adding a “D” mintmark to a Philadelphia coin — authentication is essential.\nThinking of selling?\nWe buy coins and bullion in person at our NYC Diamond District counter.\nGet a free quote →\nSee the full\ndimes value guide\n, or\nShop US silver coins →\nMore:\nall coin values\n·\nsilver price history\n·\ngold/silver ratio",
